// [test]
// spec = ["§4.4", "§6.2", "§18.1"]

// S-748 (a) (W4-05 U3a): a chain of 300 aliases and the E0307 `impl` at its head: the check ends in a short time.
// The type of the `impl` is found by following the right sides of the aliases to the declaration (an alias is
// replaced by its right side, §4.4), and the members of the `impl` are names after the name of that type
// (§18.1), so the member of the direct `impl` of the type that repeats a name is E0304, and the `impl` of the
// alias has its E0307 only. The first chain is written in the order of the aliases (`Fwdk = Fwd(k-1)`, the head is
// the last, the `impl` is after the chain) and the second in the opposite order (`Backk = Back(k+1)`, the head is the
// first, the `impl` is before the chain). The chain of 20000 aliases is a Rust test of the check, not a case
// (R-298, W4-05).

pub struct S {
  x: I32,
}

